Day 30. You are on the roof of your tower, sitting on the only way in. Five thousand gallons of water behind you, two days of food, and a radio that will not stop saying the stadium is safe.

This is days 31 to 60. What the figure on the bank roof was pointing at. Why the water turns on you. How to get a rope across a street full of the dead. And what was really broadcasting all this time.

Fiction, built on real facts: stored water needs a one-minute rolling boil, clear bottles in full sun disinfect water in about six hours, lean meat alone will not keep you alive, and the first line across the Niagara gorge in 1848 went over by kite.

